<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="445f8c5f">&lt;p&gt;
    Test scenarios are derived from defined requirements, business process, use cases, user stories and any other relevant
    information that captures solution functionality. In most cases, at least one scenario is developed for every testable
    requirement.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    When performing this task, consider the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What&amp;nbsp;functionality of the&amp;nbsp;solution needs to be verified?&amp;nbsp;This is often the description of the test
        scenario.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are multiple scenarios required to validate&amp;nbsp;a requirement?
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="63690993"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="fbd8f64e"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="142c9e25"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="dc88da75">To translate solution requirements&amp;nbsp;relevant to interactions and&amp;nbsp;behaviors between integrated components&amp;nbsp;into
testable components.</attribute>
